cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this archive, please cite both the article and the archive.
title: >-
  A Differential Theory of Quality-Resource Trade-offs for AI Model Selection:
  The Multiresource Frontier and Its Minimax Price
abstract: >-
  Data, analysis code and results reproducing every number, table and figure in
  the article, its Online Appendix and its technical report. The archive carries
  117 published quality-resource frontiers over eight corpus labels - image
  classification, distribution shift, neural architecture search, tabular
  learning, hyperparameter optimisation, materials property prediction and
  medical imaging - together with a per-item co-failure panel and language-model
  factorial grids. The pipeline reads the channel-depth curve off each frontier
  without fitting it, tests the two structural hypotheses against nulls matched
  to each frontier's own design, window and residual scale, scores the selection
  rules in current use against the derived price, and measures the size of the
  selection decision with no objective function at all. Every analytic identity
  is verified symbolically or at 40 to 50 digits.
